silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_10_alternatives_dual_computational_sections_03_computational_algorithmic_concrete_anchor_17_PathLawceqra#pathlaw_c_eq_r_a silm:hasLongDescription "The PathLaw_c_eq_r_a is the commuting path equation: Cat anchor equals refinement composed with DomesticCat-Cat embedding r. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'PathLaw_c_eq_r_a', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
